# Causal Inference & Synthetic Control for Algorithmic Pricing

## 1. Project Overview

This project analyzes the impact of algorithmic pricing strategies on revenue using Causal Inference and Synthetic Control Methods.

The main objective is to understand whether a price change leads to an actual increase in revenue and to estimate the causal impact of the pricing intervention.

The project combines Python, SQL-based analytical concepts, statistical methods, and Power BI to evaluate pricing performance across different regions.

## 2. Dataset Description

- Dataset: `project1_algorithmic_pricing_synthetic_dataset.csv`
- Data Type: Synthetic / Simulated Dataset
- Total Records: 540 rows
- Time Period: January 1, 2025 – June 29, 2025
- Regions: North, South, West
- North: Treatment Region
- South and West: Control / Donor Regions
- Intervention Date: May 1, 2025

The dataset contains pricing, competitor pricing, units sold, revenue, marketing spend, promotional activity, treatment, and period information.

**Note:** This is a simulated teaching dataset, not real company data.

