## 5. Causal Inference Methods

### Difference-in-Differences (DiD)
Used to estimate the revenue impact of the pricing intervention by comparing treatment and control regions.

### Double Machine Learning (DML)
Used to estimate the causal effect of pricing while controlling for other variables.

### Synthetic Control Method (SCM)
Created a synthetic version of the North region using South and West as donor regions to estimate what North's revenue might have been without the intervention.

### Causal DAG
Used DoWhy concepts to represent relationships between pricing, revenue, and potential confounding variables.

## 6. Synthetic Control & Robustness Testing

- Compared actual North revenue against synthetic North revenue.
- Evaluated donor weights.
- Tested South-only and West-only donor scenarios.
- Calculated pre-intervention Mean Squared Prediction Error (MSPE).
- Evaluated post-intervention revenue gaps.
- Compared alternative donor combinations.

Baseline donor weights:
- South: 50%
- West: 50%

Baseline results:
- Pre-intervention MSE: 36,627,510.23
- Pre-intervention RMSE: 6,052.07
- Post-intervention Average Gap: 2,537.58
- Cumulative Revenue Gap: 152,254.85

